{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:bounded-grant-preserves-status-and-checkpoint-continuity", "statement": "One bounded operation grant may cover its declared construction, status and checkpoint sequence. Record actual role transitions in the existing carrier; a status change alone needs no fresh grant or rehash of an unchanged subject. Resolve changed operation, subject, territory, authority or validity conditions before the affected effect, and preserve Executive mutation restrictions. A preservation checkpoint may retain unfinished or unaccepted work under its exact grant with predecessor, included territory, concurrent-writer disposition and durable evidence location; it supplies no acceptance, promotion or publication. A restart explains why retained repair is insufficient, which obligations and evidence survive and which causal assumptions change. Reconstructability supplies no restart authority.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#checkpoint-continuation-progress-and-churn", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#construction-assessment-and-delegation", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#reconstruction-litmus"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:closed-result-reuse-preserves-required-independence", "statement": "Reuse an unchanged closed result only after checking exact applicability. A material input change or declared revising observation invalidates the affected result before reliance, preserving predecessor/successor and demonstrably independent survivors. Required independent evaluations may share valid mechanical evidence but still acquire sufficient exact evidence and supply their own judgment under the actual independence conditions.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#return-a-closed-result", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:closure-is-satisfied-obligations-not-review-occurrence", "statement": "A claim completes only when every applicable declared obligation is satisfied by valid evidence for its exact subject/basis/scope, required J/O is present and applicable, and no active non-closure condition remains. Evidence existence, closed indeterminacy, a successful tool or a review event cannot satisfy a missing condition. Existing owners decide reserved acceptance; an authorized Writer may record a sufficient bounded result when no independent/reserved condition applies, retaining actual sprint-close and design obligations.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#applicability-and-required-results", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/REFERENCE_FRAME_METHOD.md#result-conjunction", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#closure", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#condition-based-closure-and-reuse", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:closure-reuse-retains-independent-progress", "statement": "Reuse valid evidence and J/O for unchanged obligations. A material counterexample or changed evidence/basis invalidates the affected claim and dependent results before reliance. Retain unrelated observations as bounded repricing input without automatic reopening or work expansion. Closure recording preserves exact evaluated scope, satisfied conditions, evidence and surviving residual obligations.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#condition-based-closure-and-reuse"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:computed-facts-judgments-and-rulings-retain-owners", "statement": "C records reproducible facts and sufficient declared rule application; J records only unresolved semantics or materiality; O remains a ruling of its actual owner. None creates operation, admission or decision authority or a new calculus kind.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#computed-classification-and-treatment", "stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/TICKET_METHOD.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:computed-result-reuse-invalidates-affected-dependencies", "statement": "After checking exact applicability, reuse valid C across roles, conversations and resumptions. Changed request, candidate, basis, owner/root, projection, accepted trace, rule, configuration or material evidence invalidates affected claims before reliance. Retain predecessor/successor identities, changed inputs, surviving facts and affected J dependencies; recompute the wider frontier where independence is unproved.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/SPEC_METHOD.md#computed-classification-and-treatment"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:executive-mutation-needs-prior-writer-transition", "statement": "Executive performs no candidate, Product, worktree or implementation mutation. Before effects, the actor explicitly records a separate Worker/Writer activation with exact grant, subject and write territory. Tool access, small/reversible/test-only edits, later recording or later delegation cannot supply or retroactively authorize that transition; changing role supplies no independent assessment.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#executive-attention-evaluation-and-action"]}
{"uri": "urn:stdo-representation:a-c-text:clause:executive-promotion-constraints", "statement": "Executive blocks a valid mandatory-claim falsification governed by a non-waivable hard stop regardless of priority, does not mechanically block a below-cutoff finding without a hard stop, returns an out-of-claim observation for bounded repricing or re-entry rather than claim-relative blocking, and reactivates or retains indeterminate any unsupported technical assessment instead of rewriting Reviewer evidence.", "source_refs": ["stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.1/standards/STDO_REFERENCE_FRAME_BASELINE.md#executive-promotion-constraint-projection"]}
